{"task":"Offer to put bin/ldev on the PATH, in the shell the user actually runs","goals":"Stop the installer printing a line nobody runs, without guessing at a startup file it could get silently wrong","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:29Z","body":"The installer has always ended by printing an `export PATH=...` line for the reader to\ncopy, and on this machine that line was never run: `ldev` was not on the PATH at all, so\nevery command the installer's own closing report suggested had to be typed as a full path.\nAn installer that asks for sudo to write a LaunchDaemon and an /etc/resolver file can\nreasonably offer to append one line to a startup file.\n\nThe offer names the file and shows the exact line before writing anything, and declining\nprints the command to run by hand — the same shape as every other root-owned step here.\n\nPicking the file is the part worth care, because getting it wrong fails SILENTLY: the line\nlands in a real file, the installer reports success, and the shell still cannot find ldev.\nSo the shell decides, and only shells whose startup file AND syntax are known get an offer:\n\n  zsh   ~/.zshrc\n  bash  ~/.bash_profile, falling back to ~/.profile — NOT ~/.bashrc. macOS Terminal opens\n        login shells, and a login bash reads .bash_profile and pointedly does not read\n        .bashrc, which is the classic way to make this quietly not work on a Mac.\n  fish  ~/.config/fish/config.fish, and the line is `fish_add_path`, because fish is not\n        POSIX and `export PATH=\"...:$PATH\"` is a syntax error in it. fish_add_path is also\n        idempotent, so re-running cannot stack duplicates the way the export line would.\n  ksh   ~/.kshrc\n\nAnything else gets the line printed rather than written to a file guessed at. $SHELL is\nread rather than the running shell, because $SHELL is the LOGIN shell — what a new\nterminal window will start — and the shell running install.sh is bash either way.\n\nTwo cases that are not \"append the line\":\n\n  - `ldev` already resolves to this checkout: say so and do nothing.\n  - `ldev` resolves to a DIFFERENT checkout: appending would not change which one wins,\n    since the existing PATH entry comes first, so it names the one that answers instead of\n    appearing to have fixed something.\n\nRe-running is safe: it greps the startup file for the bin path first, and the test asserts\nthat what gets written is what that grep looks for, so the idempotence check cannot drift\naway from the line it guards.\n\nThe README's disclosure table said \"Nothing is written anywhere else\", which this makes\nuntrue, so the shell startup file is now a row in it — marked as only happening if the\nprompt is accepted — and the Uninstall section names the `# ldev` marker line and the four\ncandidate files instead of saying \"drop bin/ from your PATH\".\n\ntest/path-setup.test.sh covers all of it without an install or sudo: nine assertions over\nthe four known shells, the empty answer for an unknown one, .bash_profile winning over\n.bashrc when both exist, .profile when neither does, both syntaxes, and the idempotence\ngrep matching the written line.\n","parent_commit":"5a35d53904f88027d0e63d12e7248a5f0b207ebc","repo":"brave-cedar-fb33","pct":"86","tasks":[{"id":"detect","content":"Pick the startup file from the login shell: zsh, bash (.bash_profile not .bashrc), fish, ksh; empty for unknown","status":"completed"},{"id":"syntax","content":"fish_add_path for fish, export PATH for POSIX shells","status":"completed"},{"id":"offer","content":"Show the file and the exact line, confirm before writing, print the command when declined","status":"completed"},{"id":"idempotent","content":"Skip when already on PATH; name the winner when a different checkout shadows it; no duplicate lines on re-run","status":"completed"},{"id":"tests","content":"test/path-setup.test.sh — 9 assertions, no install or sudo needed","status":"completed"},{"id":"docs","content":"README Install section, the disclosure table row, Uninstall, and the Tests listing","status":"completed","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:08:36.006Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"},{"id":"rehome-run","content":"Run ldev rehome against the three real WordPress sites","status":"pending","responsibility":"bryce","human_reason":"Rewrites live site data, not ldev's own files: 16,224 database rows for seasonal-drops alone, plus WP_HOME/WP_SITEURL in wp-config.php. The command deliberately refuses to run without a terminal to confirm on, so an agent cannot execute it and should not be given --yes on someone's real databases. It backs up the database and copies wp-config.php before touching either half, and prints the two commands that undo it. Bryce runs it per site: seasonal-drops, matsu, matsu-dev. The tool itself is delivered and tested in 130f207.","created_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z","status_at":"2026-09-09T19:22:30.481Z"}],"agent":"claude-code","changelog":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_quality":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","vulnerabilities":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","code_style_suggestions":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","reusability":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","system_compatibility":"Unreviewed (agent unavailable).","sessions":[{"provider":"claude","id":"3e8f56a2-7837-42a5-adfb-4e072f3876ee","title":"https://sites.ldev/ (or any other name I put) doesn't auto redirect to the projects dashboard","linked_at":"2026-09-10T01:14:29Z"}],"review_run":{"state":"did_not_run","at":"2026-09-10T01:14:29Z","attempts":1,"reason":"Review skipped at the caller's request (--no-review / automatedReview: false)."}}
